   "description": "This data product is a map of the average illumination by the solar disc of the Lunar South Pole at a resolution of 60 m/pix by 60 m/pix, true at the pole in polar stereographic (spherical) projection. The calculations are based on the LOLA elevation map LDEM_85S_060M and are described in [MAZARICOETAL2011]. The values are continuous between 0 (permanent shadow) and 1, and indicate the percentage of timesteps where each pixel was sunlit (by any fraction of the solar disc). Note a scaling was applied to fit the data in the INT16 value range. This label describes an IMG file in the form of a binary resampling with pixel registration.",
